---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import dadabase from '../assets/portfolio/dad-a-base.jpg';
import bakery from '../assets/portfolio/bakery-shell.jpg';
import PortfolioCard from '../components/PortfolioCard.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<main>
		<h1>My Projects</h1>
		<PortfolioCard
			title="The Dad-a-base"
			href="https://jokes.tylerbaker.dev"
			src={dadabase}
			alt="A 90s-inspired website with a red brick background. A header with a wooden background texture shows a joke that says 'When I am stresed I like to iron clothes. It is a great way to let off steam.'"
			tech="Hono + JSX, SVG graphics, Sqlite"
			ps="P.S., I am hosting this one on my homelab! It's running from my Raspbery Pi!"
			github="https://github.com/btylerh7/the-dad-a-base"
		>
			<p>
				This website was heavily inspired by the 1990s Geocities era of the internet. It
				features lots of custom SVGs that I made myself while learning how to make cool
				shapes and textures with SVGs by hand. The bricks, the wooden backgrounds, and even
				the clipboard icon were all made by me by hand!
			</p>
		</PortfolioCard>
		<PortfolioCard
			title="Bakery Shell"
			src={bakery}
			alt="A screenshot of a terminal window with the classic windows hill background, showing various terminal commands being run, such as 'ls' and 'cat'"
			tech="Rust, rustyline"
			github="https://github.com/btylerh7/bakery-shell"
			ps="P.S., I did most of this with the Rust standard library! The auto-complete required me to pull in a library, but I went as far as I could!"
		>
			<p>
				This project was made as a part of me using the{' '}
				<a href="https://codecrafters.io" target="_blank">
					Codecrafters
				</a>{' '}
				project "Build your own Shell". However, Codecrafters is not a traditional
				"tutorial" site, and this project is built by me. Codecrafters tells you what
				feature to add next, and you build that out however you see fit. You also choose
				your programming language, and I opted to go with Rust.
			</p>
			<p>
				Just a sample of some concepts I built: I built a custom parser, multiple shell
				builtins, auto-complete, and the ability to run external programs that are on the
				system path.
			</p>
		</PortfolioCard>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	main {
		color: white;
	}
</style>
